From bfa1eab786d6c9eb33066acac4d969ca2d9e981a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 09:54:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH]  Add optional OSMC startup splash video

  Play a short branding clip once when Kodi starts, gated by a new
  "lookandfeel.startupvideo" setting (Settings > Interface > Other),
  disabled by default.

  A fixed-framerate clip (25/30fps) is matched to the display's 50/60Hz
  refresh so the correct one plays without any resolution/refresh change.
  The mode switch that playback would normally trigger is suppressed for
  this single clip via a new CPlayerOptions::preventRefreshSwitch flag,
  passed through a "preventrefreshswitch" CFileItem property and honoured
  in CVideoPlayer::OpenVideoStream, so the global "Adjust display refresh
  rate" setting is never modified or restored.

  Playback is dispatched via TMSG_MEDIA_PLAY from CApplication::Initialize,
  so it runs on the main loop without blocking startup. An OEM clip
  (/usr/share/osmc/splash_oem_*) overrides the stock clip (splash_osmc_*)
  when present. The setting's user-facing strings (#40801/#40802) are
  provided downstream in OSMC's strings-osmc.po.

Signed-off-by: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
---
